<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint-Florentin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint-Florentin is a small town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yonne-river">Yonne</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, where the Armance meets the Armançon. Near it in 898 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-the-justiciar">Richard the Justiciar</a>, count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/autun">Autun</a>, defeated a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> army, a victory that strengthened his claim to lead the region that became the Duchy of Burgundy. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> church is known for its stained glass.</p></div>
